@*
    Checkout, at "/checkout".

    THE ONE RULE THIS PAGE HAS TO RESPECT. The catalog browses, searches, filters and sorts
    from a static file with the API and the database switched off. Checkout cannot: it needs a
    server. So the API is reached LAZILY — nothing is fetched until this page has already
    painted — and while the shop is starting the page says so, with a retry, rather than
    showing a spinner that looks broken. A shopper who never presses Checkout wakes nothing.

    THE IDEMPOTENCY KEY IS THE POINT OF THE SCREEN, and where it is stored is what makes it
    work. It lives in CheckoutState, which outlives this component, so every retry of a failed
    submit carries the same string and the server answers a repeat by handing back the order the
    first send created. It is replaced in exactly one situation — after a 402, where an order
    already belongs to it — and that decision is stated once, on CheckoutResult.ConsumedTheKey,
    rather than re-derived here.

    EVERY DOCUMENTED ANSWER GETS ITS OWN WORDS. 201 created, 202 still settling, 200 replay,
    402 declined, 402 never finished, 409 stock, 409 price, 400 refused, and no answer at all.
    Collapsing any two of those would be the page lying about something a shopper has to act on:
    whether money moved, whether stock is being held, and whether trying again is safe.
*@
@page "/checkout"
@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
@using VelaCommerce.Storefront.Cart
@using VelaCommerce.Storefront.Checkout
@implements IDisposable
@inject HttpClient Http
@inject CartState Cart
@inject CartDrawerState Drawer
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@inject IServiceProvider Services

<PageTitle>Checkout &middot; Vela Commerce</PageTitle>

<nav class="vc-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a class="vc-crumbs__link" href="">Catalog</a>
    <span class="vc-crumbs__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span>Checkout</span>
</nav>

<div class="vc-hero">
    <span class="vc-eyebrow">Checkout</span>
    <h1 class="vc-section-title">Place your order</h1>
    <p class="vc-lede">
        The shop reads your cart, revalidates every price against the live catalog and works out
        the total itself &mdash; no number on this page is trusted. There is no card to enter:
        this build ships its own payment gateway, and you choose below what it should do.
    </p>
</div>

@if (!Cart.IsLoaded && Cart.ErrorMessage is { Length: > 0 } cartError)
{
    @* The API is asleep, unreachable, or answered with something unusable. Honest, and
       recoverable in place: the cart is the only thing missing and one button asks again. *@
    <div class="vc-alert vc-alert--error" role="alert">
        <h2 class="vc-alert__title">@cartError</h2>
        <p class="vc-alert__body">
            Your cart lives on the server, so checkout cannot start until the shop answers. The
            catalog is a static file and keeps working either way &mdash; nothing you have added
            has been lost.
        </p>
        @if (Cart.ErrorDetail is { Length: > 0 } cartDetail)
        {
            <details class="vc-alert__detail">
                <summary>Technical detail</summary>
                @cartDetail
            </details>
        }
        <div class="vc-alert__actions">
            @if (Cart.CanRetry)
            {
                <button type="button" class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary" @onclick="RetryCartAsync">Try again</button>
            }
            <a class="vc-btn" href="">Back to the catalog</a>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else if (!Cart.IsLoaded)
{
    <div class="vc-waking" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="vc-waking__pip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="vc-waking__body">
            <p class="vc-waking__title">@(Cart.IsWaking ? "Waking the shop up" : "Reading your cart")</p>
            <p class="vc-waking__note">
                The API sleeps when nobody is buying anything, so the first request after a quiet
                period waits for it to start. This is the only part of the shop that needs it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else if (Cart.IsEmpty)
{
    <div class="vc-empty">
        <span class="vc-eyebrow">Nothing to buy</span>
        <h2 class="vc-empty__title">Your cart is empty</h2>
        <p class="vc-empty__body">
            There is nothing to check out. If you have just placed an order that is expected: a
            completed checkout empties the cart in the same transaction that creates the order.
        </p>
        <div class="vc-alert__actions">
            <a class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary" href="">Back to the catalog</a>
        </div>
    </div>
}
else
{
    @* Validated once per render rather than once per field, so five inputs do not each build
       their own copy of the same answer. *@
    _errors = _showErrors ? Draft.Validate() : NoErrors;

    <div class="vc-checkout">
        <form class="vc-checkout__main" @onsubmit="SubmitAsync" @onsubmit:preventDefault novalidate>

            @if (_result is { Succeeded: false } failure)
            {
                <div class="vc-alert @AlertModifier(failure) vc-checkout__result"
                     role="alert"
                     tabindex="-1"
                     @ref="_resultAlert">
                    <h2 class="vc-alert__title">@Headline(failure)</h2>
                    <p class="vc-alert__body">@Explanation(failure)</p>

                    @if (failure.Problem?.Detail is { Length: > 0 } serverDetail)
                    {
                        @* The server's own wording, not a paraphrase. "Country must be an ISO
                           alpha-2 code" is the domain's sentence and names the rule better than
                           anything this page could re-derive from the outside. *@
                        <p class="vc-alert__body vc-alert__body--quoted">@serverDetail</p>
                    }

                    @if (failure.Problem?.PriceChanges is { Count: > 0 } changes)
                    {
                        <ul class="vc-conflict">
                            @foreach (var change in changes)
                            {
                                <li class="vc-conflict__row">
                                    <span class="vc-conflict__name">@change.DisplayName</span>
                                    <span class="vc-conflict__sku vc-tabular">@change.Sku</span>
                                    @if (change.NoLongerSold)
                                    {
                                        <span class="vc-tag vc-tag--signal">No longer sold</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span class="vc-conflict__prices vc-tabular">
                                            <s>@Money(change.Was)</s>
                                            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                                            <span class="vc-conflict__now">@Money(change.Now)</span>
                                            @if (change.Difference is { } difference)
                                            {
                                                <span class="vc-conflict__delta">@Signed(difference)</span>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    }

                    @if (failure.Problem?.Shortfall is { } shortfall)
                    {
                        <ul class="vc-conflict">
                            <li class="vc-conflict__row">
                                <span class="vc-conflict__name">@shortfall.DisplayName</span>
                                <span class="vc-conflict__sku vc-tabular">@shortfall.Sku</span>
                                <span class="vc-conflict__prices vc-tabular">
                                    <span>asked for @shortfall.Requested</span>
                                    @if (shortfall.Available is { } available)
                                    {
                                        <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                                        <span>about @available free</span>
                                    }
                                </span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                        @if (shortfall.Available is not null)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-alert__detail">
                                That free count is advisory. It was read after the reservation failed, so
                                somebody else may have taken more of it since; the number that actually
                                decided this sat inside one conditional UPDATE and never left the database.
                            </p>
                        }
                    }

                    @if (failure.Problem?.Payment is { } gateway)
                    {
                        <dl class="vc-gateway">
                            <div class="vc-gateway__row">
                                <dt class="vc-gateway__key">Gateway said</dt>
                                <dd class="vc-gateway__value">
                                    @gateway.Outcome@(gateway.DeclineReason is { Length: > 0 } reason ? $" — {reason}" : "")
                                </dd>
                            </div>
                            <div class="vc-gateway__row">
                                <dt class="vc-gateway__key">Reference</dt>
                                <dd class="vc-gateway__value vc-tabular">@gateway.GatewayReference</dd>
                            </div>
                        </dl>
                    }

                    @if (failure.Detail is { Length: > 0 } clientDetail)
                    {
                        <details class="vc-alert__detail">
                            <summary>Technical detail</summary>
                            @clientDetail
                        </details>
                    }

                    <div class="vc-alert__actions">
                        @if (failure.Outcome is CheckoutOutcome.Interrupted)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary" disabled="@_submitting" @onclick="AttemptAsync">
                                Try again
                            </button>
                        }
                        @if (failure.Outcome is CheckoutOutcome.PriceMoved or CheckoutOutcome.OutOfStock)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="vc-btn" @onclick="OpenCart">Open the cart</button>
                        }
                        @if (failure.StrandedOrderNumber is { Length: > 0 } stranded)
                        {
                            <a class="vc-btn" href="@($"order/{stranded}")">Open order @stranded</a>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            }

            @if (Cart.HasPriceChanges || Cart.HasUnavailableLines)
            {
                @* Said before the button is pressed rather than after. Every cart response already
                   reports the captured price beside the live one, so letting a shopper submit into
                   a certain 409 would mean withholding an answer this page is holding. *@
                <div class="vc-alert vc-checkout__warning" role="status">
                    <h2 class="vc-alert__title">This cart will be refused as it stands</h2>
                    <p class="vc-alert__body">
                        The shop never reprices a cart quietly, so a line that has moved since you added
                        it stops the checkout instead of changing what you pay. Remove and add these
                        again in the cart to accept the current price.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="vc-conflict">
                        @foreach (var line in Cart.Lines)
                        {
                            @if (line.PriceChanged || !line.StillInCatalog)
                            {
                                <li class="vc-conflict__row" @key="line.Sku">
                                    <span class="vc-conflict__name">@line.ProductName</span>
                                    <span class="vc-conflict__sku vc-tabular">@line.Sku</span>
                                    @if (!line.StillInCatalog)
                                    {
                                        <span class="vc-tag vc-tag--signal">No longer sold</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span class="vc-conflict__prices vc-tabular">
                                            <s>@MoneyFormatter.Format(line.UnitPrice)</s>
                                            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                                            <span class="vc-conflict__now">@MoneyFormatter.Format(line.CurrentUnitPrice)</span>
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                </li>
                            }
                        }
                    </ul>
                    <div class="vc-alert__actions">
                        <button type="button" class="vc-btn" @onclick="OpenCart">Open the cart</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }

            <section class="vc-checkout__section">
                <div class="vc-checkout__section-head">
                    <h2 class="vc-checkout__section-title">Shipping address</h2>
                    @if (Draft.IsUntouched)
                    {
                        <button type="button" class="vc-btn vc-btn--quiet vc-btn--sm" @onclick="FillSample">
                            Fill in a sample address
                        </button>
                    }
                </div>

                <div class="vc-formgrid">
                    <div class="vc-field vc-formgrid__wide">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-recipient">Recipient</label>
                        <input class="vc-input" id="vc-ck-recipient" type="text" autocomplete="name"
                               aria-invalid="@Invalid(nameof(AddressDraft.Recipient))"
                               aria-describedby="@Describe(nameof(AddressDraft.Recipient))"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.Recipient" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        @if (Error(nameof(AddressDraft.Recipient)) is { } recipientError)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-field__error" id="vc-ck-recipient-error">@recipientError</p>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field vc-formgrid__wide">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-line1">Address line 1</label>
                        <input class="vc-input" id="vc-ck-line1" type="text" autocomplete="address-line1"
                               aria-invalid="@Invalid(nameof(AddressDraft.Line1))"
                               aria-describedby="@Describe(nameof(AddressDraft.Line1))"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.Line1" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        @if (Error(nameof(AddressDraft.Line1)) is { } line1Error)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-field__error" id="vc-ck-line1-error">@line1Error</p>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field vc-formgrid__wide">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-line2">
                            Address line 2 <span class="vc-field__optional">optional</span>
                        </label>
                        <input class="vc-input" id="vc-ck-line2" type="text" autocomplete="address-line2"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.Line2" @bind:event="oninput" />
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-city">City</label>
                        <input class="vc-input" id="vc-ck-city" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2"
                               aria-invalid="@Invalid(nameof(AddressDraft.City))"
                               aria-describedby="@Describe(nameof(AddressDraft.City))"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.City" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        @if (Error(nameof(AddressDraft.City)) is { } cityError)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-field__error" id="vc-ck-city-error">@cityError</p>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-region">
                            State or region <span class="vc-field__optional">optional</span>
                        </label>
                        <input class="vc-input" id="vc-ck-region" type="text" autocomplete="address-level1"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.Region" @bind:event="oninput" />
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-postal">Postal code</label>
                        <input class="vc-input vc-tabular" id="vc-ck-postal" type="text" autocomplete="postal-code"
                               aria-invalid="@Invalid(nameof(AddressDraft.PostalCode))"
                               aria-describedby="@Describe(nameof(AddressDraft.PostalCode))"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.PostalCode" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        @if (Error(nameof(AddressDraft.PostalCode)) is { } postalError)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-field__error" id="vc-ck-postal-error">@postalError</p>
                        }
                    </div>

                    <div class="vc-field">
                        <label class="vc-label" for="vc-ck-country">Country</label>
                        <input class="vc-input vc-tabular" id="vc-ck-country" type="text" autocomplete="country"
                               maxlength="2" placeholder="US" spellcheck="false"
                               aria-invalid="@Invalid(nameof(AddressDraft.CountryCode))"
                               aria-describedby="@CountryDescribedBy()"
                               disabled="@_submitting"
                               @bind="Draft.CountryCode" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        <p class="vc-field__hint" id="vc-ck-country-hint">Two letters, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2.</p>
                        @if (Error(nameof(AddressDraft.CountryCode)) is { } countryError)
                        {
                            <p class="vc-field__error" id="vc-ck-country-error">@countryError</p>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="vc-checkout__section">
                @* The @ on Value is load-bearing: a string-typed component parameter written
                   without it is passed as the literal text "_checkout.PaymentScenario", which
                   matches no scenario and silently leaves every radio unchecked. *@
                <PaymentScenarioPicker Value="@_checkout.PaymentScenario"
                                       ValueChanged="OnScenarioChanged"
                                       Disabled="_submitting" />
            </section>

            <div class="vc-checkout__submit">
                <button type="submit" class="vc-btn vc-btn--primary vc-checkout__place" disabled="@_submitting">
                    @(_submitting ? "Placing your order…" : "Place order")
                </button>

                <p class="vc-checkout__submit-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">
                    @if (_waking)
                    {
                        <span>
                            The shop is still starting up. Nothing has been charged, and this attempt keeps
                            its reference &mdash; whatever happens next, it cannot become two orders.
                        </span>
                    }
                    else if (_submitting)
                    {
                        <span>Reserving stock, revalidating prices and asking the gateway.</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span>No card is taken and nothing is charged. The gateway is simulated.</span>
                    }
                </p>
            </div>
        </form>

        <aside class="vc-checkout__aside" aria-label="Order summary">
            <div class="vc-summary">
                <h2 class="vc-summary__title">Your order</h2>

                <ul class="vc-summary__lines">
                    @foreach (var line in Cart.Lines)
                    {
                        <li class="vc-summary__line" @key="line.Sku">
                            <div class="vc-summary__line-main">
                                <span class="vc-summary__name">@line.ProductName</span>
                                <span class="vc-summary__meta">
                                    @if (line.VariantName is { Length: > 0 } variantName)
                                    {
                                        <span>@variantName</span>
                                        <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                                    }
                                    <span class="vc-tabular">@line.Sku</span>
                                    <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
                                    <span class="vc-tabular">&times;@line.Quantity</span>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                            <PriceTag Money="line.LineTotal" />
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>

                <hr class="vc-rule" />

                <div class="vc-subtotal">
                    <span class="vc-subtotal__label">Subtotal</span>
                    <PriceTag Money="Cart.Subtotal" Large="true" />
                </div>

                <p class="vc-summary__note">
                    Shipping and tax are worked out by the shop when the order is placed, from prices it
                    revalidates itself. The exact total is on the confirmation, and it is the figure the
                    gateway is asked for.
                </p>

                <hr class="vc-rule" />

                @* Shown rather than hidden. This reference is the whole reason a double submit
                   cannot become two orders, and a demo about idempotency that never shows the key
                   is a demo about nothing. *@
                <div class="vc-readout vc-readout--stacked vc-summary__key">
                    <span class="vc-readout__label">Attempt reference</span>
                    <span class="vc-readout__value">@_checkout.IdempotencyKey</span>
                </div>
                <p class="vc-summary__note">
                    Sent with the order as its idempotency key. Every retry of this attempt carries the
                    same one, so the shop answers a repeat by handing back the order it already made.
                </p>
            </div>
        </aside>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// How long one checkout attempt is given.
    /// <para>
    /// Generous, because the first request after a quiet period is paying for a container to start,
    /// a connection pool to open and a payment to be authorised. Deliberately one attempt rather
    /// than an automatic retry loop: the key would make an automatic retry safe, but this is
    /// somebody's money and the decision to send it again belongs to them. The button that does it
    /// is one press away and says what it does.
    /// </para>
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan SubmitDeadline = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(45);

    /// <summary>How long a request may run before the page admits the shop is asleep. The same notice the cart uses.</summary>
    private static readonly TimeSpan WakeNotice = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2);

    private static readonly IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> NoErrors =
        new Dictionary<string, string>(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    private CheckoutApiClient _api = default!;
    private CheckoutState _checkout = default!;
    private ElementReference _resultAlert;

    private IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> _errors = NoErrors;
    private CheckoutResult? _result;
    private bool _showErrors;
    private bool _submitting;
    private bool _waking;
    private bool _focusResult;

    private AddressDraft Draft => _checkout.Address;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _api = new CheckoutApiClient(Http);

        // Resolved rather than injected, so a missing AddStorefrontCheckout() registration costs a
        // draft that does not survive navigation instead of a checkout page that throws. See
        // CheckoutServiceCollectionExtensions for the one line that should be in Program.cs.
        _checkout = Services.GetService<CheckoutState>() ?? new CheckoutState();

        Cart.Changed += OnCartChanged;
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            // AFTER the first render, never before it. Awaiting the cart in OnInitializedAsync would
            // hold this page blank for as long as a sleeping API takes to answer, which is exactly
            // the spinner-that-looks-broken this shop is built to avoid. The shell paints first,
            // says what it is waiting for, and fills in.
            await Cart.EnsureLoadedAsync();
        }

        if (_focusResult)
        {
            _focusResult = false;
            await FocusAsync(_resultAlert);
        }
    }

    private void OnCartChanged() => StateHasChanged();

    private Task RetryCartAsync() => Cart.RetryAsync();

    private void OpenCart() => Drawer.Open();

    private void OnScenarioChanged(string hint) => _checkout.PaymentScenario = hint;

    private void FillSample() => Draft.FillWithSample();

    private async Task SubmitAsync()
    {
        // Errors appear on the first submit and stay live from then on, so a field corrected while
        // its message is on screen loses the message as it is typed into.
        _showErrors = true;

        if (Draft.Validate().Count > 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        await AttemptAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Sends the attempt. Reachable twice — from the submit button and from Try again on an
    /// interrupted result — and that is the design: the second press carries the same key as the
    /// first, which is what makes it safe.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task AttemptAsync()
    {
        if (_submitting || Cart.IsEmpty)
        {
            return;
        }

        _submitting = true;
        _waking = false;
        _result = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        CheckoutResult result;

        try
        {
            using var deadline = new CancellationTokenSource(SubmitDeadline);

            var body = new PlaceOrderBody(
                Draft.ToBody(),
                _checkout.IdempotencyKey,
                _checkout.PaymentScenario);

            var work = _api.PlaceOrderAsync(body, deadline.Token);

            // A call that is slow rather than failing is a cold start, and saying so beats a
            // spinner. The delay is deliberately not tied to the deadline token: a stray
            // two-second timer costs nothing, and cancelling it would mean the notice never
            // appeared on the one path it exists for.
            if (await Task.WhenAny(work, Task.Delay(WakeNotice)) != work)
            {
                _waking = true;
                StateHasChanged();
            }

            result = await work;
        }
        catch (Exception exception)
        {
            // The client turns every documented refusal into a result rather than an exception, so
            // reaching here means something unforeseen. It is reported as interrupted because that
            // is what it is: the state of the order is unknown, and the same key is the way to find
            // out safely. An unhandled exception on a payment screen would show the Blazor error
            // bar and leave the shopper with no idea whether they had bought anything.
            result = new CheckoutResult(
                CheckoutOutcome.Interrupted,
                Order: null,
                Problem: null,
                $"{exception.GetType().Name}: {exception.Message}");
        }
        finally
        {
            _submitting = false;
            _waking = false;
        }

        if (result.Succeeded && result.Order is { } order)
        {
            // The gateway's answer exists only on this response — it is persisted nowhere for a
            // later GET to find — so it is handed to the order page rather than dropped.
            _checkout.RememberReceipt(order);

            // The server emptied the cart inside the same transaction that created the order, so
            // this is the client catching up rather than a second decision. Clear() is a no-op on an
            // already-empty cart and the DELETE it sends is idempotent. The accepted edge is a 200
            // replay of an older order, where anything added since is discarded with it; a
            // CartState.ReloadAsync() would be the better seam and does not exist yet.
            Cart.Clear();

            Nav.NavigateTo(OrderPage(order));
            return;
        }

        // A 402 means an order already belongs to this key — cancelled, or pending and unpaid — so
        // sending it again would replay that dead order forever rather than buy anything. Every
        // other failure created nothing and leaves the key unspent, which is what makes Try again
        // safe on the interrupted path.
        if (result.ConsumedTheKey)
        {
            _checkout.StartNewAttempt();
        }

        _result = result;
        _focusResult = true;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The storefront's own link to the order rather than the API's <c>retrievalPath</c>: the same
    /// signed token, pointing at a page a shopper can read and bookmark.
    /// </summary>
    private static string OrderPage(OrderDocument order) =>
        $"order/{Uri.EscapeDataString(order.OrderNumber)}?token={Uri.EscapeDataString(order.RetrievalToken)}";

    private string? Error(string field) => _errors.TryGetValue(field, out var message) ? message : null;

    private string? Invalid(string field) => Error(field) is null ? null : "true";

    private string? Describe(string field) => Error(field) is null ? null : FieldErrorId(field);

    /// <summary>The country field always has a hint to point at, and sometimes an error as well.</summary>
    private string CountryDescribedBy() =>
        Error(nameof(AddressDraft.CountryCode)) is null
            ? "vc-ck-country-hint"
            : "vc-ck-country-hint vc-ck-country-error";

    private static string FieldErrorId(string field) => field switch
    {
        nameof(AddressDraft.Recipient) => "vc-ck-recipient-error",
        nameof(AddressDraft.Line1) => "vc-ck-line1-error",
        nameof(AddressDraft.City) => "vc-ck-city-error",
        nameof(AddressDraft.PostalCode) => "vc-ck-postal-error",
        _ => "vc-ck-country-error",
    };

    private static string Money(MoneyDocument? money) =>
        money is null ? "—" : MoneyFormatter.Format(money.Amount, money.Currency);

    /// <summary>A price difference with its sign kept, so "the bargain expired" and "it got cheaper" read differently.</summary>
    private static string Signed(MoneyDocument difference) =>
        (difference.Amount > 0 ? "+" : "") + MoneyFormatter.Format(difference.Amount, difference.Currency);

    private static string AlertModifier(CheckoutResult result) =>
        result.Outcome is CheckoutOutcome.Declined or CheckoutOutcome.Rejected
            ? "vc-alert--error"
            : "vc-alert--notice";

    /// <summary>
    /// The headline for a refusal: the server's own title where it sent one, because it names the
    /// rule better than a re-derivation would, and a written fallback where nothing came back.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Headline(CheckoutResult result) =>
        result.Problem?.Title is { Length: > 0 } title
            ? title
            : result.Outcome switch
            {
                CheckoutOutcome.Interrupted => "The shop did not answer",
                CheckoutOutcome.Declined => "The payment was declined",
                CheckoutOutcome.OutOfStock => "Not enough stock left",
                CheckoutOutcome.PriceMoved => "Prices have changed since these items were added",
                _ => "That checkout could not be accepted",
            };

    /// <summary>
    /// What it means, in the two terms a shopper actually needs: whether money moved, and what to do
    /// next. Distinct per outcome on purpose — a shared "please try again" would be wrong for four
    /// of these six.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Explanation(CheckoutResult result) => result.Outcome switch
    {
        CheckoutOutcome.Declined =>
            "Nothing was charged. The order has been cancelled and its stock released, and your cart is "
            + "exactly as it was. This attempt has been given a new reference, because the previous one "
            + "now belongs to the cancelled order — so you can change the simulated outcome below and "
            + "place a new one.",

        CheckoutOutcome.NotCompleted =>
            "Nobody refused the payment and nobody made it, so an order exists, is unpaid, and is still "
            + "holding its reserved stock until that reservation lapses. Nothing was charged. This "
            + "attempt has a new reference; the order that was created is linked below.",

        CheckoutOutcome.PriceMoved =>
            "Nothing was created and nothing was charged. The shop refuses to reprice a cart quietly in "
            + "either direction, so a line that has moved stops the checkout and asks you to look. Remove "
            + "and add these lines again in the cart to accept the current price.",

        CheckoutOutcome.OutOfStock =>
            "Nothing was created and nothing was charged. Somebody else reserved the last of one of these "
            + "while this order was being placed. Lower the quantity in the cart, or take the line out, "
            + "and place the order again.",

        CheckoutOutcome.Rejected =>
            "The shop refused the request itself, so no order exists and nothing was charged. The line "
            + "below is the shop's own wording: it names the rule that was broken.",

        _ =>
            "No answer arrived, so whether the order was created is genuinely unknown — it may exist, and "
            + "may even be paid. This is what the attempt reference is for: Try again sends the same one, "
            + "and the shop answers a repeat by handing back the order it already made rather than making "
            + "a second. It cannot charge you twice.",
    };

    /// <summary>Focus, defensively. A stale element reference must never be the thing that takes a payment screen down.</summary>
    private static async Task FocusAsync(ElementReference element)
    {
        try
        {
            await element.FocusAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // The message is on screen and readable with a pointer either way.
        }
    }

    public void Dispose() => Cart.Changed -= OnCartChanged;
}
